{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Have you anyone else here.</b> Its plain sense: Is there anyone else yours in this city besides your wife and your daughters who are in the house?" "<b>Son-in-law and your sons and your daughters.</b> And if you have a son-in-law or sons and daughters, take them out of the place." "<b>ובניך.</b> The sons of your daughters who are married. And the midrash: since they commit such villainy — <b>מי לך</b> — an opening of the mouth, to argue in their favor? All night long he had been pleading good things on their behalf; read in it מי לך פה — 'what mouth have you [for them]!'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:26.140775071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}